# Scratch that has reached the root before and should not again.
#
# SIGN_TEST.txt was one line reading "signed test", committed while verifying
# that commit signing worked, and it sat in the root of a public repository for
# months. purge_v7.py was a one-off migration for the v7 release, still present
# at 13.7 where a reader could mistake dead code for something runnable.
#
# Neither was a mistake at the moment it was written. Both were mistakes the
# moment they stopped being needed and nothing removed them.
*_TEST.txt
SIGN_TEST*
purge_v*.py
*.bak
*.orig
scratch/
tmp/
